From 9f27f48713cd0516bb7faae4e41eda63d2e994aa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:56:12 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Add Loyalty Reward Home notification

Detects, server-side, when a completed transaction crosses a
customer's loyalty points balance from below the configured reward
threshold to at/above it, and opens one persistent Home notification
per reward cycle.

- New table public.loyalty_reward_notifications (migration
  20260930010000) plus a trigger on the existing loyalty_point_events
  ledger insert (private.detect_loyalty_reward_threshold). Detection
  reuses the ledger's existing guards, so cancelled, deleted,
  incomplete or non-qualifying transactions never produce a
  notification.
- Idempotent by construction: a partial unique index on
  source_event_id/source_redemption_id plus a partial unique index on
  (customer_id) WHERE status='active', both enforced via
  `on conflict do nothing`. Refreshes, retries and realtime
  reconnects are pure reads and cannot create duplicates.
- RLS: any active Owner or Staff can read; no client write path
  exists at all (writes only happen through the SECURITY DEFINER
  trigger and public.redeem_loyalty_reward). Redemption stays
  Owner-only, unchanged.
- public.redeem_loyalty_reward now resolves the matching
  notification on redemption and, if the remaining balance still
  clears the threshold, opens a new active notification for the next
  reward cycle (documented in the migration's comments).
- Home UI: new LoyaltyRewardHomeCard (styled after OnHoldHomeCard),
  backed by useLoyaltyRewardNotifications (client-side join of
  notifications + customers + live balances, with a realtime
  subscription). Owner sees a "Open Loyalty & Redeem" action;
  Staff sees notification + customer details only. No card renders
  when nothing has qualified.
- OwnerDashboard now honors ?tab=loyalty for the Home card's deep
  link, guarded by the existing Owner-only tab check.
- tests/backend/test.mjs: 15 new pglite tests covering below/at/above
  threshold, refresh idempotency, concurrent-duplicate rejection at
  the DB constraint level, Owner/Staff/anon RLS, Staff cannot
  redeem/resolve, cancelled/deleted transactions, redemption
  resolving the alert and audit trail, a later new reward cycle,
  On Hold regression, and that SMS/PhilSMS code, config and column
  grants are untouched. Full suite: 80 passed, 0 failed.

Scope: Home notification only. No SMS/PhilSMS/provider work, no
Production deploy, no `supabase db push` was run.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DeFV6HNfuxKwGxuKyxSEx9
